  "_comment": "Cross-collector parity golden. BOTH collector/ (Node) and collector-go/ scan corpus/ and must produce exactly these figures. Paths use forward slashes; each suite normalises its platform separator before comparing. See test-fixtures/collector-parity/README.md. schemaVersion and columns were added after issue #31: the two collectors' schemas had silently diverged (Go on 4, Node on 7), and Go's unconditional version stamp rewrote a Node-migrated database downwards, which made Node's next migrate throw on a duplicate column. toolCallSourceFiles was added for issue #32: row counts alone could not see that the Go collector left source_file_rel NULL for every tool call, so downstream resolveDispatchEvidence reported no file-touch correlation. usageSourceFiles was added at v8: usage_events now records which transcript each turn came from, which is what makes 'has this file already been counted?' answerable at all. dispatches was added for issues #107 and #65: the Go collector wrote 0 for absent usage, no exit_state/dispatch_status, and no severity, session_id or agent_id, while Node stored NULL and scored the run; the per-id dispatches block pins every one of those columns for failed, killed, unknown, injected-body, no-subagent_type and median-slow runs.",
